---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description = 'Roslyn-powered C# tooling for developer CLI workflows, coding agents through MCP, and architecture and complexity rule enforcement in CI.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Roslyn Tools" description={description} activePath="/">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="site-shell hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Developer CLI · Agent MCP · CI checks</p>
        <h1>Semantic C# tools for developers, agents, and CI.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">
          Navigate whole solutions, preview refactorings, and enforce repository
          rules with one Roslyn-powered engine and structured results.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/docs/getting-started/">Use the CLI</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/automation-and-mcp/">Connect with MCP</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/ci/">Enforce CI rules</a>
        </div>
        <div class="package-callout" aria-label="Roslyn Tools executables">
          <span>CLI + MCP host</span>
          <code>rt · roslyn-tools-mcp</code>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="code-window" aria-label="Roslyn Tools example">
        <div class="code-window-bar">
          <span>Three ways to work</span>
          <span class="code-status">compiler-backed</span>
        </div>
        <pre><code><span class="code-muted"># CLI: inspect a type</span>
rt inspect describe BookingService \
  --solution MyApp.slnx --trust-repository

<span class="code-muted"># MCP: an agent follows callers</span>
relationships {'{'}
  <span class="code-string">"symbol"</span>: <span class="code-string">"BookingService.ReserveAsync"</span>,
  <span class="code-string">"mode"</span>: <span class="code-string">"callers"</span>,
  <span class="code-string">"solution"</span>: <span class="code-string">"MyApp.slnx"</span>
{'}'}

<span class="code-muted"># CI: enforce your .rt/ci.json policy</span>
rt ci check --solution MyApp.slnx \
  --json --trust-repository</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="lineage-section">
    <div class="site-shell lineage-row">
      <p>Built on Roslyn. Whole-solution context. Shared operations. Structured results.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/command-reference/">Explore the commands <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="principles-section" id="principles">
    <div class="site-shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Three use cases</p>
        <h2>From local exploration to enforced rules.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article>
          <span class="principle-number">01</span>
          <h3>Developer CLI</h3>
          <p>Inspect symbols, trace references, analyze impact, and preview solution-wide refactorings from your terminal.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/getting-started/">Start with the CLI <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="principle-number">02</span>
          <h3>Coding agents through MCP</h3>
          <p>Give agents semantic tools with bounded, structured results and explicit repository trust.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/automation-and-mcp/">Connect your agent <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="principle-number">03</span>
          <h3>CI rule enforcement</h3>
          <p>Check architecture boundaries and method complexity against a checked-in policy. Fail the pipeline when rules are violated.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/ci/">Configure CI checks <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="boundary-section">
    <div class="site-shell boundary-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Powered by Roslyn</p>
        <h2>One semantic engine across your workflow.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="boundary-copy">
        <p>
          The CLI, MCP host, and CI checks share application services and command
          metadata. Explore locally, work with an agent, and enforce agreed rules
          in your pipeline using the same understanding of your C# solution.
        </p>
        <p>IDE integration is planned as a future fourth use case; it is not available yet.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/discovery/">Find your next command <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
